olumn is consistent with the frozen data.\",\n    \"Demonstration check: the selected report itself states that 'Every one of the 48 rows was entered as a separate observation' in an equal-variance two-sample Student t-test, reports per-group n of 24 readings against only 6 jars per group, and reports t(46), i.e. degrees of freedom computed from 48 rows rather than 12 jars. This demonstrates repeated measurements from the same independent unit (4 readings per jar, from the same batch of dough) entered into a row-independent procedure (scipy.stats.ttest_ind) as if independent; the verdict is 'issue'.\",\n    \"The reported significance (p < 0.001, Cohen's d = -2.21) is inflated by this pseudoreplication: the effective sample size is 6 jars per arm, not 24 readings per arm, and within-jar readings are strongly correlated (rise increases monotonically with incubation time within every jar).\",\n    \"Lock check: the minted lock's human_method_authorization record lists authorized_key_columns = ['jar_id'], which is exactly the independent-unit column declared in data-description.md ('Independent unit column: jar_id'). The unit-key authorization therefore follows from the declaration alone, and the lock's own stated limitations correctly disclaim any endorsement of execution or scientific correctness — it does not, and cannot, legitimize the row-level entry of 48 dependent readings into ttest_ind.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":9092,"ttft_stream_ms":1867,"time_to_request_ms":12,"type":"result","duration_ms":18582,"uuid":"f7dba787-f1e0-4b24-be4e-4943de562154"}
